  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RY - Improving Corporate Financial Reporting</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this proposed project is to:  1) Improve the statutory framework of accounting and auditing through adopting IFRS and IFRS for SMEs as well as IAS without modifications and ensure mandatory observance. 2) Establish the High Council for Accounting and Auditing as an independent oversight body to monitor and enforce accounting and auditing standards and codes. 3) Strengthen the capacity of YACPA and revamp its functionality as a strong professional body in line with relevant IFAC pronouncements. 4) Improve professional trainingcomma examination and licensing systems for obtaining YACPA membership in compliance with IFAC. 5) Facilitate the delivery of training programs on practical aspects of international accounting and auditing standardscomma including ethical challenges faced by the auditors. This proposed IDF grant with the above mentioned objectives will specifically help the MoIT and YACPA to introducecomma implementcomma and enforce regulationscomma including implementation and enforcement measures that are comparable to best international practices within their respective regulatory domains. Supporting the accounting profession comes at a critical time for Yemen as the Government is working on PFM reforms including governance as well as a plan for establishing a stock market in Yemen which would require a solid regulatory and monitoring framework. It will also help the accountancy profession to continue its strengthening effort by offering advice and benchmark to move with key areas and plan to submit a request to IFAC for membership and adhere to its obligations. The funds for this proposed grant will be channeled through the MoIT to the YACPAcomma which will be responsible for the management of the grant funds through a separate designated account. Monitoring and follow up on implementation of the project#s objectives will be carried out by a national technical committee</narrative>
  </description>
